# DataShield Project Rules for Cursor / AI Assistants

You are assisting on "DataShield: Django Privacy & Compliance Platform".
Topic: Personal Data Protection & Decree 13/2023 / GDPR Compliance in Django.
Team: 
- Le Duy Khanh (Team Lead, Branch: main)
- Nguyen Van Hieu (Member, Branch: nguyen-van-hieu)

CRITICAL INSTRUCTIONS (ZERO TOLERANCE):
1. MANDATORY: ALWAYS read `TASKS.md` first to check task assignments and file boundaries.
2. ALWAYS read and inspect existing code in `privacy/models.py`, `privacy/services.py`, `privacy/views.py`, and `config/settings.py` before modifying or proposing code.
3. DO NOT mix file modifications across member boundaries without explicit approval.
4. NEVER bypass PostgreSQL Row-Level Security (RLS) or `TenantScopedModel`.
5. NEVER allow mutation or deletion of `AuditEvent` (immutable SHA-256 hash ledger).
6. Strictly follow Python 3.12+ type annotations and clean architecture.
7. Ensure all existing tests pass via `pytest` before completing any task.
